  "result": "Fixed. `IntRange` clamping with an open bound returned a value outside the range.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` returned `bound - dir` when the bound was open. The direction `dir` is `+1` for the min bound and `-1` for the max bound, so the step went the wrong way. With `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)`, the input `-5` clamped to `-1`, which is outside the range.\n\n**Fix:** Changed it to `bound + dir`, so the value steps into the range from the open bound. That gives `1` for the min case and `4` for `max_open` at 5.\n\n**Tests:** Added four cases to `tests/test_types.py` covering min-open and max-open clamping, including inputs past the bound and the bound itself. `tests/test_types.py` and `tests/test_info_dict.py` pass (73 passed, 2 skipped).\n\nI didn't add a changelog entry in `docs/changes.md`. Let me know if you want one.",
